            <ArticleTitle>Crohn's-associated chronic recurrent multifocal osteomyelitis responsive to infliximab.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>541-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a case of chronic recurrent clavicular osteomyelitis in association with Crohn disease. Steroid therapy resulted in partial remission; however, intractable shoulder pain and an enlarging clavicular mass subsequently recurred. Infliximab therapy resulted in significant improvement in the degree of bone pain and resolution of the large sclerotic clavicular lesion.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
